We actually designed delete.retention.ms to address the lost tombstone issue. The following is the doc. Basically, if a consumer is lagging, it's expected to catch up within delete.retention.ms to avoid missing a tombstone. If you expect a consumer to be down for a longer time, you could increase delete.retention.ms. Note that when a tombstone is removed, all records with the same key before that tombstone have already been removed.
